  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nOur dangerous heat wave continues as the region remains under\na 596 dm H5 ridge. With 850 mb temperatures hovering around\n23-25C (around the 99th percentile), high temperatures should\nhave no trouble reaching the lower to middle 90s, despite dew\npoint temperatures approaching 80 degrees. This will yield daily\npeak heat index values of 105 to 115 degrees through Friday. \n\nEnsemble guidance is showing the ridge starting to break down\nbeginning this weekend, and this will allow mentionable\nprecipitation chances to return. Schc PoPs return to the \nforecast as soon as Thursday, but look to increase to chc levels\nfor the Fourth of July into next week. We will need to keep a\nclose eye on the potential for \"ridge rider\" MCS activity\nimpacting the region as the H5 ridge diminishes. Predictability\non these kind of events is usually on the lower side at this\nrange, so adjustments to the precipitation forecast are\npossible in the next day or two.",
